IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bdm-registration`

-- Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the
-- situation as parameters, for one deployment that serves every seat.
--
-- ROLES (the seat as a parameter). Every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question
-- about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input, so the form never asks those inputs.
--   - `I am a parent registering my child's birth` -- the baseline's first seat (Part 3: ss 12-23).
--   - `I am marrying, or have married` -- the baseline's seat for Part 6 (ss 37-39).
--   - `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` -- the baseline's seat for Part 7 (ss 40-48).
--   - `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` -- new: the person ss 42, 45, 46 and 47 put
--     their duties on. The baseline encodes those duties as what the family is owed; this role asks them as its own.
-- The Registrar, the coroner, the courts and the hospital's chief executive are never a seat: what they must or may do appears
-- only as what it means for the person asking. The doctor (ss 12, 44) is not a role in this layer (see NOTES.md).
-- The certificate and fee questions (ss 55, 57, 70; Regulations r 4) and s 2 arise for the parent, the couple and the family.
--
-- SITUATIONS (the graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's fact
-- straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` without reading anything else when the situation does not
-- hold. The questions of one situation share one input, with the same name, type and @desc:
--   - `my child was born in Western Australia` (BOOLEAN; parent): the three s 12 questions arise only for a birth in the State
--     (s 12(2) "When a child is born in the State"), so FALSE gives `does not arise for you`; the s 13(3)-(6) question arises
--     only for a birth outside it (a birth in the State must be registered, s 13(1)), so TRUE does. "Must my child's birth be
--     registered" takes it as an ordinary input, since it arises either way.
--   - `where the person died` (`Where the person died`; family and funeral director): s 42 applies "If a person dies in the
--     State", so the four questions of s 42 and the two of s 44 (whose certificate goes to "the person who is responsible under
--     section 42") arise only for `in Western Australia`; the s 40(4)-(6) question only for the other three values. "Must the
--     death be registered" takes it as an ordinary input.
--   - `what has been done with the remains` (`What is done with the remains`, the baseline's own type; family and funeral
--     director): the s 45/46(a) questions arise only once there has been a disposal (not for `kept, not yet disposed of` or
--     `removal of cremated remains from the State`, which the baseline counts as no disposal); s 46(b) only for
--     `removal of the uncremated remains from the State`; s 47 only for `kept, not yet disposed of`. The s 4 question takes it
--     as an ordinary input.
--
-- The rules are the baseline's (`bdm-registration.l4`); this layer calls them and restates none. Where the baseline's seat asks
-- a question here, the answer is the baseline export's answer wrapped in the answer type. No exported question takes a DEONTIC
-- or EVENT input. Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers, as the baseline writes them.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am a parent registering my child's birth`
    `I am marrying, or have married`
    `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died`
    `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains`

DECLARE `Where the person died` IS ONE OF
    `in Western Australia`
    `in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia`
    `elsewhere in Australia`
    `outside Australia`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Number of days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `days` HAS `how many` IS A NUMBER

-- Dates are YYYYMMDD numbers, as in the baseline (not the DATE of the graffiti layer).
DECLARE `Date answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `by` HAS `the last day, written YYYYMMDD` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Who notifies the birth` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the birth is notified by` HAS `the notifier` IS A `Birth notifier`

DECLARE `Who registers the birth` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the birth is registered by` HAS `the registrant` IS A `Birth registrant`

DECLARE `Who settles the name answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the name` HAS `who settles it` IS A `Who settles the name`

DECLARE `What is lodged` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `lodge` HAS `the document` IS A `Marriage document`

DECLARE `Who notifies the death` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the death is notified by` HAS `the death notifier` IS A `Death notifier`

DECLARE `Who certifies the death` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the cause of death is certified by` HAS `the doctor` IS A `Certifying doctor`

DECLARE `Who registers the death answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the death is registered by` HAS `the registering person` IS A `Who registers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `The situations a question arises in`

-- Each helper lists every value of its situation and has no OTHERWISE: on the stable l4 a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE takes the
-- OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing (graffiti finding 31), so the cases could not show the input unread.
GIVEN `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the death was not in the State` IF
    CONSIDER `where the person died`
    WHEN `in Western Australia` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `elsewhere in Australia` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `outside Australia` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `what has been done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there has been no disposal to notify` IF
    CONSIDER `what has been done with the remains`
    WHEN `cremation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `burial` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `burial at sea` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `placing in a mausoleum or other permanent resting place` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `removal of the uncremated remains from the State` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `removal of cremated remains from the State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `kept, not yet disposed of` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `what has been done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remains were not removed uncremated` IF
    CONSIDER `what has been done with the remains`
    WHEN `cremation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `burial` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `burial at sea` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `placing in a mausoleum or other permanent resting place` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removal of the uncremated remains from the State` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `removal of cremated remains from the State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `kept, not yet disposed of` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `what has been done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remains have been disposed of` IF
    CONSIDER `what has been done with the remains`
    WHEN `cremation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `burial` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `burial at sea` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `placing in a mausoleum or other permanent resting place` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removal of the uncremated remains from the State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removal of cremated remains from the State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `kept, not yet disposed of` THEN FALSE

§§ `For the parent, the couple and the family`

§§§ `s 2 -- does this Act govern the event`

@export Does this Act govern the registration of a birth, marriage or death on this date (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 2)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the date of the event` IS A NUMBER @desc The date of the birth, marriage or death, written YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this Act govern the registration of an event on this date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`Does this Act govern the event` `the date of the event`)
    WHEN `I am marrying, or have married` THEN `yes if` (`Does this Act govern the event` `the date of the event`)
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN `yes if` (`Does this Act govern the event` `the date of the event`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 55, 57, 70 and Regulations r 4 -- certificates and fees`

@export Can I be given a certified copy of the registration (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) ss 55, 57)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I stated my reason for wanting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you stated the reason for your interest in the entry
      `the Registrar accepts my reason as adequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar accepts that you have shown an adequate reason and will issue
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be given a certified copy of the registration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be given a certificate` `I stated my reason for wanting it` `the Registrar accepts my reason as adequate`)
    WHEN `I am marrying, or have married` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be given a certificate` `I stated my reason for wanting it` `the Registrar accepts my reason as adequate`)
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be given a certificate` `I stated my reason for wanting it` `the Registrar accepts my reason as adequate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the prescribed fee for this service, in dollars (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Regulations 1999 (WA) r 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A `Registry service` @desc The service you are asking for
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the prescribed fee for this Registry service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN amount (`What is the fee` `the service`)
    WHEN `I am marrying, or have married` THEN amount (`What is the fee` `the service`)
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN amount (`What is the fee` `the service`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What will I pay for this service, after any remission (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Regulations 1999 (WA) r 4; Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 70)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the service` IS A `Registry service` @desc The service you are asking for
      `with priority processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you ask for the certificate to be processed in priority (item 11, added to the fee)
      `the amount the Registrar remits` IS A NUMBER @desc The dollars of the fee the Registrar remits under s 70 (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What will I pay for this Registry service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN amount (`What will I pay` `the service` `with priority processing` `the amount the Registrar remits`)
    WHEN `I am marrying, or have married` THEN amount (`What will I pay` `the service` `with priority processing` `the amount the Registrar remits`)
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN amount (`What will I pay` `the service` `with priority processing` `the amount the Registrar remits`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Penalties -- ss 12, 16, 42, 44-47`

@export What is the most the person responsible can be fined for this offence, in dollars (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) ss 12(2), 16(1), 42, 44, 45, 46, 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS AN Offence @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the person responsible can be fined for this offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN amount (`What is the most that can be fined` `the offence`)
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN amount (`What is the most that can be fined` `the offence`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN amount (`What is the most that can be fined` `the offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the parent registering a child's birth`

§§§ `s 12 -- the hospital or attendant notifies the birth`

@export Who must notify the Registrar of my child's birth (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child was born in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child was born in Western Australia
      `the hospital involved` IS A Hospital @desc The hospital where the child was born, or to which the child was brought within 24 hours of birth; no hospital otherwise
      `the child was stillborn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was stillborn (at least 20 weeks or 400 grams, with no sign of life)
      `a doctor or midwife attended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a doctor or midwife attended the birth
GIVETH A `Who notifies the birth`
`Who must notify the Registrar of my child's birth` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN
        IF NOT `my child was born in Western Australia`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the birth is notified by` (`Who must notify my child's birth` `the hospital involved` `the child was stillborn` `a doctor or midwife attended`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By what date must my child's birth be notified to the Registrar (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 12(2); one month, read as to the same day of the next month)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child was born in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child was born in Western Australia
      `the date of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's date of birth, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`By what date must my child's birth be notified to the Registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN
        IF NOT `my child was born in Western Australia`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by` (`By what date must the birth be notified` `the date of birth`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was my child's birth notified to the Registrar in time (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child was born in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child was born in Western Australia
      `the date of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's date of birth, YYYYMMDD
      `the date of the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The date the hospital, doctor, midwife or attendant gave the Registrar notice, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was my child's birth notified to the Registrar in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN
        IF NOT `my child was born in Western Australia`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Was the birth notified in time` `the date of birth` `the date of the notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 13 -- must my child's birth be registered here`

-- Arises for every birth, so the place of birth is an ordinary input here (the same name, type and @desc as the situation).
@export Must my child's birth be registered under this Act (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 13(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child was born in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child was born in Western Australia
      `a State court ordered registration here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a State court has ordered the birth registered in Western Australia
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my child's birth be registered under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`Must my child's birth be registered` `my child was born in Western Australia` `a State court ordered registration here`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- A birth in the State must be registered (s 13(1)), so whether it may be is asked only of a birth outside it. The flight or
-- voyage and the birth abroad are both outside the State, so the baseline's inputs are kept as they are.
@export May my child's birth be registered here although it need not be (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 13(3)-(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my child was born in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your child was born in Western Australia
      `another court determined it should be registered here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court of another State or of the Commonwealth determined that the birth should be registered in Western Australia
      `the Registrar considers it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar considers it appropriate to register it on that determination
      `born on a flight or voyage to Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was born in an aircraft or vessel travelling to an airport or port in the State
      `born abroad and to become a resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was born outside Australia and is to become a resident of the State
      `already registered in another State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the birth is already registered under another State's law
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my child's birth be registered here although it need not be` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN
        IF `my child was born in Western Australia`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May my child's birth be registered here` `another court determined it should be registered here` `the Registrar considers it appropriate` `born on a flight or voyage to Western Australia` `born abroad and to become a resident` `already registered in another State`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 15, 16 -- who registers the birth, and by when`

@export Who is responsible for having my child's birth registered (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the child is a foundling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a foundling (found, parents unknown)
GIVETH A `Who registers the birth`
`Who is responsible for having my child's birth registered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `the birth is registered by` (`Who must have the birth registered` `the child is a foundling`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I sign the birth registration statement alone (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 15(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the reason` IS A `Reason the other parent does not sign` @desc Why the other parent is not signing
      `the Registrar is satisfied it is impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied that it is impracticable for the other parent to join, for that reason
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I sign the birth registration statement alone` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`May I sign the statement alone` `the reason` `the Registrar is satisfied it is impracticable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days after the birth do we have to lodge the birth registration statement (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 16(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`How many days after the birth do we have to lodge the birth registration statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `days` `How many days do we have to register the birth`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is our birth registration statement in time (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 16(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days after the birth` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the birth the statement was, or will be, lodged
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is our birth registration statement in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`Is our statement in time` `days after the birth`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the Registrar still accept our birth registration statement if it is late (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 16(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days after the birth` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the birth the statement was, or will be, lodged
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Registrar still accept our birth registration statement if it is late` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Registrar accept our statement` `days after the birth`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most we can be fined for not lodging the birth registration statement within 60 days (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 16(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days after the birth` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the birth the statement was, or will be, lodged
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most we can be fined for not lodging within 60 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN amount (`What is the most we can be fined for registering late` `days after the birth`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 18 -- will both parents be named`

@export Will both parents be named in the Register (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 18(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the application` IS A `How the parents apply` @desc Whether both parents apply, or one applies alone
      `the Registrar is satisfied the other does not dispute it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied the other parent does not dispute the details
      `a State court ordered it or found the parentage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a State court ordered the details included or found who the parent is
      `another court so determined and the Registrar thinks it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another State's or the Commonwealth's court so determined and the Registrar considers it appropriate
      `a law lets the Registrar presume the parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any law entitles the Registrar to presume who the parent is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Will both parents be named in the Register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`Will both parents be named` `the application` `the Registrar is satisfied the other does not dispute it` `a State court ordered it or found the parentage` `another court so determined and the Registrar thinks it appropriate` `a law lets the Registrar presume the parent`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 19, 22, 23 -- the child's name`

@export May the Registrar change my child's surname on my application (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 19(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `both parents apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both parents make the application together
      `the other parent has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child's other parent has died
      `the other parent is missing and siblings bear the surname` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other parent cannot be found and other children of the same parents are registered in the proposed surname
      `the Registrar thinks the surname prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is of the opinion that the surname is a prohibited name
      `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in years
      `the child consents or cannot understand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a child of 12 or more: whether the child consents, or cannot understand the change
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Registrar change my child's surname on my application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`May my child's surname be changed` `both parents apply` `the other parent has died` `the other parent is missing and siblings bear the surname` `the Registrar thinks the surname prohibited` `the child's age` `the child consents or cannot understand`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must we give our child a name in the birth registration statement (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 22(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the child was stillborn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was stillborn (at least 20 weeks or 400 grams, with no sign of life)
      `the child died within 28 days of birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child, born alive, died within 28 days
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must we give our child a name in the birth registration statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`Must we name our child` `the child was stillborn` `the child died within 28 days of birth`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must our child's surname be the same as a parent's (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 22(3)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must our child's surname be the same as a parent's` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` `Must the surname be a parent's`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must our child's name have both a surname and a given name (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 22(3)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must our child's name have both a surname and a given name` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` `Must the name have a surname and a given name`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Registrar give our child a name we did not choose (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 22(4)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Registrar thinks the name prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is of the opinion that the name is a prohibited name
      `we lodged together and cannot agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both parents lodged and satisfied the Registrar that they cannot agree on the name
      `the Family Court resolved the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Family Court has resolved a dispute about the child's name
GIVETH A `Who settles the name answer`
`Can the Registrar give our child a name we did not choose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `the name` (`Who settles our child's name` `the Registrar thinks the name prohibited` `we lodged together and cannot agree` `the Family Court resolved the dispute`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I the right person to apply to change my child's given names (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 23(2)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `who signed` IS A `Who signed the statement` @desc Who signed the child's birth registration statement
      `who applies` IS A `Who applies` @desc Who is applying for the change
      `one parent has since died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the parents has died since the statement was lodged
      `neither parent can act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both parents have since died, cannot be found or cannot exercise parental responsibility
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I the right person to apply to change my child's given names` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`Am I the right person to apply under s 23` `who signed` `who applies` `one parent has since died` `neither parent can act`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I change my child's given names (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 23; once, within 12 months of the birth)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the date of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's date of birth, YYYYMMDD
      `the date of the application` IS A NUMBER @desc The date of the application, YYYYMMDD
      `the right person applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application is made by the person s 23(2)(c) names (see the question above)
      `applied under s 23 before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application to change the child's given names has been made before
      `the Registrar thinks a name prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is of the opinion that a requested name is a prohibited name
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I change my child's given names within the first year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent registering my child's birth` THEN `yes if` (`May I change my child's given names` `the date of birth` `the date of the application` `the right person applies` `applied under s 23 before` `the Registrar thinks a name prohibited`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the couple marrying`

§§§ `Part 6 -- ss 37-39, registering the marriage`

@export Must our marriage be registered under this Act (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 37)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `solemnized in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the marriage was solemnised in Western Australia
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must our marriage be registered under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am marrying, or have married` THEN `yes if` (`Must our marriage be registered` `solemnized in Western Australia`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is lodged to register our marriage (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 38)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `solemnized before the Marriage Act 1961 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the marriage was solemnised before the Commonwealth Marriage Act 1961 commenced
GIVETH A `What is lodged`
`What is lodged to register our marriage under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am marrying, or have married` THEN `lodge` (`What is lodged to register our marriage` `solemnized before the Marriage Act 1961 commenced`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Added (new for this role): s 38 says "A person may have a marriage registered by lodging" the certificate, a permission, and
-- its note places the lodging on the celebrant (Marriage Act 1961 (Cth) s 50(4)). Part 6 puts no duty or time limit on the
-- couple, so the answer is no.
@export Must we ourselves lodge our marriage certificate with the Registrar, by a time this Act sets (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 38 and its note; the celebrant lodges it under the Marriage Act 1961 (Cth) s 50(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must we ourselves lodge our marriage certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am marrying, or have married` THEN no
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the family, or the executor, of a person who has died`

§§§ `s 40 -- must the death be registered here`

-- Arises wherever the person died, so the place is an ordinary input here (the same name, type and @desc as the situation).
@export Must the death be registered under this Act (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 40(1), (2), (7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died` @desc Where the person died: in Western Australia; in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia; elsewhere in Australia; or outside Australia
      `a State court or coroner ordered registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a State court or a coroner in the State has ordered the death registered
      `a stillborn child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death is of a stillborn child
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the death be registered under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN `yes if` (`Must the death be registered` (NOT (`the death was not in the State` `where the person died`)) `a State court or coroner ordered registration` `a stillborn child`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- A death in the State must be registered (s 40(1)), so whether a death elsewhere may be is asked only of the other three
-- places. A death elsewhere in Australia is neither s 40(4) nor s 40(5), so the answer is no.
@export May a death that happened outside Western Australia be registered here (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 40(4)-(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died` @desc Where the person died: in Western Australia; in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia; elsewhere in Australia; or outside Australia
      `the person was domiciled or resident here, or left property here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a death outside Australia: whether the person was domiciled or ordinarily resident in Western Australia, or left property in it
      `the Registrar refuses because it is registered elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar refuses because the death is registered under another State's law
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May a death that happened outside Western Australia be registered here` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        CONSIDER `where the person died`
        WHEN `in Western Australia` THEN `does not arise for you`
        WHEN `in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`May the death be registered here` TRUE FALSE `the Registrar refuses because it is registered elsewhere`)
        WHEN `elsewhere in Australia` THEN no
        WHEN `outside Australia` THEN `yes if` (`May the death be registered here` FALSE `the person was domiciled or resident here, or left property here` `the Registrar refuses because it is registered elsewhere`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 48 -- the Registrar registers the death`

@export May the death be registered before the coroner finds the cause (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 48(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the death be registered before the coroner finds the cause of death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN `yes if` `May the death be registered before the coroner finds the cause`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Will the death certificate be marked as issued before the coronial investigation ended (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 48(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a coronial investigation is incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an inquest or other coronial investigation into the cause of death is still incomplete
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Will the death certificate be marked as issued before the coronial investigation ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN `yes if` (`Will the certificate be endorsed` `a coronial investigation is incomplete`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the family and the funeral director`

§§§ `ss 42, 43 -- who notifies the Registrar of the death, and by when`

@export Who must notify the Registrar of the death (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) ss 42, 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died` @desc Where the person died: in Western Australia; in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia; elsewhere in Australia; or outside Australia
      `the body was placed for medical education or research` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body was given to an educational or scientific institution for medical education or research
      `a coroner found a suspected death established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a coroner, at an inquest into a suspected death, found the death established
GIVETH A `Who notifies the death`
`Who must notify the Registrar of the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the death is notified by` (`Who must notify the death` `the body was placed for medical education or research` `a coroner found a suspected death established`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the death is notified by` (`Who must notify the death` `the body was placed for medical education or research` `a coroner found a suspected death established`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- New for the funeral director: the s 42(a) duty is theirs unless the body is placed with an institution (s 42(b)) or a coroner
-- is the notifying person (s 43).
@export Must I notify the Registrar of this death, and give the Registrar the doctor's certificate of cause of death (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) ss 42, 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died` @desc Where the person died: in Western Australia; in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia; elsewhere in Australia; or outside Australia
      `the body was placed for medical education or research` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body was given to an educational or scientific institution for medical education or research
      `a coroner found a suspected death established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a coroner, at an inquest into a suspected death, found the death established
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I notify the Registrar of this death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE CONSIDER `Who must notify the death` `the body was placed for medical education or research` `a coroner found a suspected death established`
             WHEN `the funeral director or other person arranging disposal` THEN yes
             WHEN `the person in charge of the institution` THEN no
             WHEN `the coroner` THEN no
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days must the death registration statement be lodged (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 42; from the date of death, or the finding or placement of the body)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died` @desc Where the person died: in Western Australia; in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia; elsewhere in Australia; or outside Australia
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`Within how many days must the death registration statement be lodged` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` `How many days to notify the death`
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` `How many days to notify the death`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was the death notified to the Registrar in time (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 42)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died` @desc Where the person died: in Western Australia; in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia; elsewhere in Australia; or outside Australia
      `days after the death, finding or placement` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the date of death (or finding or placement of the body) to the lodging of the statement
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was the death notified to the Registrar in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Was the death notified in time` `days after the death, finding or placement`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Was the death notified in time` `days after the death, finding or placement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 44 -- the doctor's certificate of cause of death`

@export Which doctor must certify the cause of death (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 44)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died` @desc Where the person died: in Western Australia; in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia; elsewhere in Australia; or outside Australia
      `the kind of death` IS A `Kind of death` @desc Whether it is the death of a person, a stillbirth or a neonatal death
      `the death must be reported to a coroner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the doctor must report the death to a coroner under s 17(3) of the Coroners Act 1996
GIVETH A `Who certifies the death`
`Which doctor must certify the cause of the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the cause of death is certified by` (`Which doctor must certify the cause of death` `the kind of death` `the death must be reported to a coroner`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the cause of death is certified by` (`Which doctor must certify the cause of death` `the kind of death` `the death must be reported to a coroner`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the doctor in breach of the 48-hour duty to certify the cause of death (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 44)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where the person died` IS A `Where the person died` @desc Where the person died: in Western Australia; in an aircraft or on a vessel on its way to Western Australia; elsewhere in Australia; or outside Australia
      `the death must be reported to a coroner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the doctor must report the death to a coroner under s 17(3) of the Coroners Act 1996
      `hours after the death` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours from the death to the certificate (or now, if none has been given)
      `another doctor gave the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another doctor has given the certificate
      `the doctor had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the doctor had reasonable cause for not being able to comply
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the doctor in breach of the 48-hour duty to certify` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is the doctor in breach of s 44` `the death must be reported to a coroner` `hours after the death` `another doctor gave the certificate` `the doctor had reasonable cause`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `the death was not in the State` `where the person died`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is the doctor in breach of s 44` `the death must be reported to a coroner` `hours after the death` `another doctor gave the certificate` `the doctor had reasonable cause`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 4, 45-47 -- disposal of the remains`

-- Arises whatever has been done, so the remains are an ordinary input here (the same name, type and @desc as the situation).
@export Is what has been done with the remains a disposal under the Act (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has been done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains` @desc What has been done with the person's remains so far: cremated, buried (on land or at sea), placed in a mausoleum or other permanent resting place, taken out of the State (uncremated, or after cremation), or not yet disposed of
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is what has been done with the remains a disposal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN `yes if` (`Is it a disposal` `what has been done with the remains`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN `yes if` (`Is it a disposal` `what has been done with the remains`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days after the disposal, or the removal from the State, must the Registrar be given notice of it (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) ss 45, 46(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has been done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains` @desc What has been done with the person's remains so far: cremated, buried (on land or at sea), placed in a mausoleum or other permanent resting place, taken out of the State (uncremated, or after cremation), or not yet disposed of
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`Within how many days must the Registrar be given notice of the disposal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `there has been no disposal to notify` `what has been done with the remains`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` (`How many days to notify the disposal` `what has been done with the remains`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `there has been no disposal to notify` `what has been done with the remains`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` (`How many days to notify the disposal` `what has been done with the remains`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was the disposal, or the removal from the State, notified to the Registrar in time (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) ss 45, 46(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has been done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains` @desc What has been done with the person's remains so far: cremated, buried (on land or at sea), placed in a mausoleum or other permanent resting place, taken out of the State (uncremated, or after cremation), or not yet disposed of
      `days after the disposal` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the disposal (or the removal from the State) to the notice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was the disposal notified to the Registrar in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `there has been no disposal to notify` `what has been done with the remains`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Was the disposal notified in time` `what has been done with the remains` `days after the disposal`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `there has been no disposal to notify` `what has been done with the remains`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Was the disposal notified in time` `what has been done with the remains` `days after the disposal`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 46(b): "within 28 days after the remains are disposed of outside the State give the Registrar notice". The baseline does not
-- encode (b); it is a helper here.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 46(b) -- days to notify the disposal outside the State` MEANS 28

@export If uncremated remains were taken out of the State, within how many days after they are disposed of there must the Registrar be given a second notice (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 46(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has been done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains` @desc What has been done with the person's remains so far: cremated, buried (on land or at sea), placed in a mausoleum or other permanent resting place, taken out of the State (uncremated, or after cremation), or not yet disposed of
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`Within how many days of the disposal outside the State must the Registrar be told` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `the remains were not removed uncremated` `what has been done with the remains`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` `s 46(b) -- days to notify the disposal outside the State`
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `the remains were not removed uncremated` `what has been done with the remains`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` `s 46(b) -- days to notify the disposal outside the State`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 47 arises only while the remains have not been disposed of; the baseline's `disposed of` is then FALSE by the situation.
@export Must the Registrar be told that the remains have not been disposed of within 30 days (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has been done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains` @desc What has been done with the person's remains so far: cremated, buried (on land or at sea), placed in a mausoleum or other permanent resting place, taken out of the State (uncremated, or after cremation), or not yet disposed of
      `days since the death` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the date of death
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Registrar be told that the remains have not been disposed of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN
        IF `the remains have been disposed of` `what has been done with the remains`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the Registrar be told the remains are not disposed of` FALSE `days since the death`)
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN
        IF `the remains have been disposed of` `what has been done with the remains`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the Registrar be told the remains are not disposed of` FALSE `days since the death`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 48 -- who registers the death`

@export Who registers the death (Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (WA) s 48(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Who registers the death answer`
`Who registers the death in the Register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am family, or the executor, of a person who has died` THEN `the death is registered by` `Who registers the death`
    WHEN `I am a funeral director, or I arrange the disposal of a person's remains` THEN `the death is registered by` `Who registers the death`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
